# OWNER REVIEW
# Grizelda on the lawn of number 4, her old house (Key 1, her test; levels/primrose/keys/grizelda_test.gd).

~ test
Grizelda: Number 4. Twelve years I lived here. I still dream about the hedges.
Grizelda: Those three are in my garden every Thursday, "looking round". They have never once bought a house.
Grizelda: Your test. Take tea with them, in the suit, and don't let them rattle you.
Nim: And if they do?
Grizelda: Then they'll talk about you for twelve years. As they do about me.
Grizelda: There's a wardrobe in my old porch. Use it.

~ verdict
Grizelda: Adequate.
Grizelda: Don't let it go to your head. Here. My Scold. You've earned the right to raise your voice.
Grizelda: One word, said properly, and every bulldog in earshot forgets he has legs.

~ after
Grizelda: The hedges are worse than I remember. Go on. They won't scold themselves.

~ verdict_world
Grizelda: Marjorie Gander. Tied to her own bench. Under her own sign.
Grizelda: Twelve years I waited to see that, and I didn't have to lift a finger.
Grizelda: Adequate. Don't let it go to your head.
[narrator] As Nim goes, Grizelda turns to Vesper, and lowers her voice.
Grizelda: She's good.
Vesper [warm]: I know.
# Grizelda's job is done: she's home at the Velvet Claw from now on (core/sisters.gd).
Vesper [warm]: Come home, Grizelda. Your throne's been cold for weeks.
Grizelda: Hmph. It had better have been dusted.

~ garden_after
Grizelda: I'm staying a while. I want to look at this a bit longer. Then home, and my own throne.
